WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 7.4 · Brand, Identity & Image
Naming and brand architecture

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Decide how your names will relate as you grow, while it is still cheap to change.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.393
Brand architecture is how the names of your organisation, programmes, products and related entities relate to each other. Deciding the logic now, while it is cheap to change, stops people losing track of you.

4
00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:28.393
Three models to choose from

5
00:00:28.393 --> 00:00:37.870
Branded house: Everything uses the master name plus a plain descriptor. For example: “[Name] Bakery” and “[Name] Training”: one name, one promise for the neighbourhood.

6
00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:47.719
Endorsed brands: Each offer has its own name, linked with “part of” or “by”. For example: The year-two shop, shown as “[Shop name], part of [Name]”.

7
00:00:47.719 --> 00:00:59.137
House of brands: Each offer has its own name with no visible link. For example: A wholesale line for cafés and canteens, kept apart from the training programme.

8
00:00:59.537 --> 00:01:00.137
Why it matters

9
00:01:00.137 --> 00:01:05.441
1. One clear logic stops audiences getting confused as you grow.

10
00:01:05.441 --> 00:01:10.004
2. Changing names later costs money, materials and recognition.

11
00:01:10.004 --> 00:01:17.048
3. A future hybrid needs an early choice: one family or distinct brands.

12
00:01:17.448 --> 00:01:18.048
What it guides

13
00:01:18.048 --> 00:01:22.981
1. How you name every new programme, product or campaign.

14
00:01:22.981 --> 00:01:27.174
2. Your visual identity: one system or several.

15
00:01:27.174 --> 00:01:33.107
3. Your registration and web addresses, checked before you commit.

16
00:01:33.507 --> 00:01:34.107
What to avoid

17
00:01:34.107 --> 00:01:40.152
Adopting a name before checking spelling, languages, web address and social handles.

18
00:01:40.152 --> 00:01:45.826
Ignoring trademarks: check with someone with a legal background before registering.

19
00:01:45.826 --> 00:01:51.389
Mixing models by accident instead of by choice.

20
00:01:51.989 --> 00:01:53.789
You map your brand architecture, now and planned.

21
00:01:53.789 --> 00:01:57.789
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:01:59.289 --> 00:02:02.389
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
